.tmp/

# A full clone of an upstream project, kept next to the `pomodoro` context only as a
# reference while that context was being written. It carries its own Git history, so
# committing it would nest a repository inside this one and hide its files behind a
# gitlink. It is a checkout, not a source of this project: the upstream URL lives in
# `docs/Pomodoro/.git/config`, and the context it informed is the code in
# `contexts/meowo-pomodoro`.
docs/Pomodoro/

# The build and server logs under `docs/` are **tracked on purpose**: `docs/acceptance.md` links to
# them as the evidence for the acceptance claims, so ignoring them would leave those links pointing
# at nothing. Their machine-specific paths were scrubbed instead — the logs stay, the home
# directory does not.
